exports[`buildPrompt > resumed turn with a quote, its page, images and the tools intro 1`] = `
"Note: you now have two tools for the documents.
You have two document tools: \`search\` (forgiving full-text search over the documents: accents, ß/ss, case and hyphenation don't matter; returns pages with excerpts) and \`read_pages\` (the exact text of a page range; page numbers are the PDF's). Use \`search\` to find where something is discussed and \`read_pages\` to read those pages, instead of opening the large text files. Search for short terms (one or two words), and try synonyms or other word forms if nothing is found.

I selected this passage on page 12:
<selection>
Hence the limit exists.
</selection>

Full text of that page for context:
<page n="12">
Lemma 3. … Hence the limit exists. …
</page>

I attached 2 images. Look at each of them with your file-reading tool:
1. /lib/d1/images/a.png
2. /lib/d1/images/b.png

Answer language: the language of my question.

